@startuml Greenfield_Infrastructure_Bootstrap

title Greenfield Infrastructure Bootstrap\nFacility iTwin → Project iTwin → First SyncSegments\nAutomated Channel and Subscription Provisioning

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam participant {
    FontSize 11
}
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #888888

actor "Project\nManager" as PM
participant "iTwin\nPlatform" as ITWIN
participant "ENG\nEngine" as ENG_E
participant "ISBM\nProvider" as ISBM
participant "REG-LOCATION\nEngine" as REG_E
participant "MMS\nEngine" as MMS_E
participant "CMS\nEngine" as CMS_E

note over ISBM
  **Pre-existing at deployment time:**
  /mndot/enterprise/sites/publication
  /mndot/enterprise/cir/request
end note

== System Startup: Engines Subscribe to Enterprise Channels ==

ENG_E -> ISBM: OpenPublicationSession\n  /mndot/enterprise/sites/publication
ISBM --> ENG_E: pub-eng-sites

REG_E -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  /mndot/enterprise/sites/publication\n  topics: ["oiie/ccom:SyncSites"]\n  listenerUrl: https://reg-engine/api
ISBM --> REG_E: sub-reg-sites

note over ENG_E, CMS_E
  At this point only two enterprise channels exist.
  No per-iTwin channels. No per-iTwin subscriptions.
  MMS and CMS have nothing to subscribe to yet.
end note

== Step 1: Project Manager Creates Facility iTwin ==

PM -> ITWIN: Create iTwin\n  class: Thing, subClass: Asset\n  type: Highway\n  name: "US Route 202"

ITWIN -> ITWIN: Assign iTwinId:\n  **aaa-111-...**

ITWIN -> ENG_E: iTwins.iTwinCreated.v1\n  iTwinId: aaa-111-...\n  class: Thing, subClass: Asset\n  parentId: (none)

activate ENG_E
ENG_E -> ITWIN: GET /iTwins/aaa-111-...
ITWIN --> ENG_E: { type: "Highway",\n  displayName: "US Route 202", ... }

ENG_E -> ENG_E: Compile SyncSites BOD\n  Site.UUID = aaa-111-...\n  Site.Type = "Highway"\n  ParentSite = (none)

ENG_E -> ISBM: PostPublication (pub-eng-sites)\n  topic: oiie/ccom:SyncSites\n  body: SyncSites (facility)
ISBM --> ENG_E: msg-001
deactivate ENG_E

ISBM -> REG_E: **webhook** /notifications/{sub-reg-sites}/msg-001
activate REG_E

REG_E -> ISBM: ReadPublication (sub-reg-sites)
ISBM --> REG_E: SyncSites BOD (aaa-111-..., Thing/Asset)

REG_E -> REG_E: Create Scope, Item, Serial,\nSystems Structure\n(see SyncSites Add workflow)

group Bootstrap per-iTwin channels for facility aaa-111-...
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/publication
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/request
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../condition/publication
end

group Open subscriptions on new facility channels
    REG_E -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication\n  topics: ["oiie/ccom:SyncSegments"]\n  listenerUrl: https://reg-engine/api
    ISBM --> REG_E: sub-reg-eng-facility
end

group Notify downstream engines: "new facility, subscribe now"
    note over REG_E
      REG-LOCATION Engine publishes a
      SyncSites to asset-config so MMS
      and CMS know to subscribe.
    end note

    REG_E -> ISBM: OpenPublicationSession\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication
    ISBM --> REG_E: pub-reg-ac-facility

    MMS_E -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication\n  topics: ["oiie/ccom:SyncSegments"]\n  listenerUrl: https://mms-engine/api
    ISBM --> MMS_E: sub-mms-facility

    CMS_E -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication\n  topics: ["oiie/ccom:SyncSegments"]\n  listenerUrl: https://cms-engine/api
    ISBM --> CMS_E: sub-cms-facility
end

REG_E -> ISBM: RemovePublication (sub-reg-sites)
deactivate REG_E

note over ISBM
  **Infrastructure after Step 1:**
  Enterprise channels (pre-existing):
    /mndot/enterprise/sites/publication
    /mndot/enterprise/cir/request

  Facility channels (just created):
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication      ← REG-LOCATION subscribed
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication     ← MMS + CMS subscribed
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/publication
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/request
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../condition/publication

  No iModel exists yet. No segments flowing.
  The facility is an empty shell with plumbing ready.
end note

|||

== Step 2: Project Manager Creates Project iTwin (Under Facility) ==

PM -> ITWIN: Create iTwin\n  class: Endeavor, subClass: Project\n  type: Highway\n  name: "Bridge 9340 Rehab"\n  parent: aaa-111-...

ITWIN -> ITWIN: Assign iTwinId:\n  **bbb-222-...**

ITWIN -> ENG_E: iTwins.iTwinCreated.v1\n  iTwinId: bbb-222-...\n  class: Endeavor, subClass: Project\n  parentId: **aaa-111-...**

activate ENG_E
ENG_E -> ITWIN: GET /iTwins/bbb-222-...
ITWIN --> ENG_E: { type: "Highway",\n  displayName: "Bridge 9340 Rehab", ... }

ENG_E -> ENG_E: Compile SyncSites BOD\n  Site.UUID = bbb-222-...\n  Site.Type = "Highway"\n  Parent context: aaa-111-...\n  (carried in ApplicationArea\n   or CIR ParentEntityID)

ENG_E -> ISBM: PostPublication (pub-eng-sites)\n  topic: oiie/ccom:SyncSites\n  body: SyncSites (project, parent=aaa-111-...)
ISBM --> ENG_E: msg-002
deactivate ENG_E

ISBM -> REG_E: **webhook** /notifications/{sub-reg-sites}/msg-002
activate REG_E

REG_E -> ISBM: ReadPublication (sub-reg-sites)
ISBM --> REG_E: SyncSites BOD (bbb-222-..., Endeavor/Project, parent=aaa-111-...)

REG_E -> REG_E: Create project Scope\n  (child of facility scope aaa-111-...)\nCreate Item, Serial,\nSystems Structure

group Bootstrap per-iTwin channels for project bbb-222-...
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication
    REG_E -> ISBM: CreateChannel\n  /mndot/bbb-222-.../construction/publication
end

group Open subscriptions on new project channels
    REG_E -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication\n  topics: ["oiie/ccom:SyncSegments"]\n  listenerUrl: https://reg-engine/api
    ISBM --> REG_E: sub-reg-eng-project

    note over REG_E
      REG-LOCATION Engine now subscribes to
      engineering channels on BOTH iTwins:
        sub-reg-eng-facility (aaa-111-...)
        sub-reg-eng-project  (bbb-222-...)
      It will process segments from each
      into the correct scope.
    end note
end

REG_E -> ISBM: RemovePublication (sub-reg-sites)
deactivate REG_E

note over ISBM
  **Infrastructure after Step 2:**
  Enterprise channels:
    /mndot/enterprise/sites/publication
    /mndot/enterprise/cir/request

  Facility channels (aaa-111-...):
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication      ← REG-LOCATION subscribed
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication     ← MMS + CMS subscribed
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/publication
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/request
    /mndot/aaa-111-.../condition/publication

  Project channels (bbb-222-...):
    /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication      ← REG-LOCATION subscribed
    /mndot/bbb-222-.../construction/publication

  Still no iModel. Still no segments.
  Both iTwins have their plumbing. REG-LOCATION
  Engine is listening on both engineering channels.
end note

|||

== Step 3: Designer Creates iModel and Publishes First Segments ==

PM -> ITWIN: Create iModel in project bbb-222-...\n  name: "Bridge 9340 Structural"

note over ITWIN
  Designer opens iModel in MicroStation,
  creates engineering elements,
  commits a Named Version.
end note

ITWIN -> ENG_E: Named Version event\n  iModelId: im-9340-struct\n  iTwinId: bbb-222-...

activate ENG_E
ENG_E -> ENG_E: Query iModel for segments\nin this Named Version:\n  TIC-106 (FedGuid: 550e8400-...)\n  FV-201  (FedGuid: 661f9511-...)

ENG_E -> ENG_E: Compile SyncSegments BOD

ENG_E -> ISBM: OpenPublicationSession\n  /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication
ISBM --> ENG_E: pub-eng-project

ENG_E -> ISBM: PostPublication (pub-eng-project)\n  topic: oiie/ccom:SyncSegments\n  body: <SyncSegments>\n    TIC-106 (FedGuid: 550e8400-...)\n    FV-201  (FedGuid: 661f9511-...)\n  </SyncSegments>
ISBM --> ENG_E: msg-003
deactivate ENG_E

ISBM -> REG_E: **webhook** /notifications/{sub-reg-eng-project}/msg-003
activate REG_E

REG_E -> ISBM: ReadPublication (sub-reg-eng-project)
ISBM --> REG_E: SyncSegments BOD

REG_E -> REG_E: Persist segments in\n**project scope** (bbb-222-...)\n  TIC-106 → pending approval\n  FV-201  → pending approval

REG_E -> ISBM: RemovePublication (sub-reg-eng-project)
deactivate REG_E

note over PM, CMS_E
  **Infrastructure complete. First segments received.**

  The entire chain — from "PM creates facility" to
  "first engineering segments land in REG-LOCATION" —
  required no human intervention beyond creating
  the iTwins and designing in MicroStation.

  Everything else was automatic:
  ✓ SyncSites events detected and processed
  ✓ Channels created for both iTwins
  ✓ Subscriptions opened dynamically
  ✓ SyncSegments published and received
  ✓ Segments persisted in the correct project scope

  Segments sit pending approval.
  When a human approves them and commissioning occurs,
  they will flow from the project scope to the facility
  scope and out to MMS and CMS via
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication
end note

@enduml
